"Linear search" and "binary search" are explicit syllabus items. Official DA papers have asked for:

- the recurrence satisfied by the worst-case number of binary-search comparisons;
- the maximum number of comparisons in an unsuccessful binary search on an array of a given size (NAT);
- the inputs on which binary search runs in $O(\log n)$ worst-case time (MSQ: sorted array, unsorted array, linked list).

